   "html_text": "Responses on behalf of EC to such arguments vary. Commenting on Stanley, Barbara Partee (2004) agrees that ‘know’ is indeed unlike expressions such as ‘tall’, but that perhaps better models are available. Nikola Kompa (2002) suggests that the context-sensitivity of ‘know’ is best understood as deriving from a sui generis sort of “unspecificity”. And Rob Stainton (2010), while sympathetic to the claim that ‘know’ is not itself context-sensitive, believes that the “spirit” of EC can be saved: if t",
